id: pm-ado-muqg
title: Closed the polynomial expression in the relation parser that a coverage edit had introduced
description: "The relation target parser originally took the final path segment by splitting on the separator. That form carries a branch no test can reach, because splitting a string always yields at least one element, and the coverage gate reported it. Replacing the split with a single unanchored expression that matched the final segment removed the branch and read as tidier, and it introduced a high-severity polynomial expression: the scan retries at every position in a run of separators. CodeQL flagged it on the first scan of the new repository.\n\nThe lesson is the interesting part. The change was made to satisfy a coverage gate rather than to change behaviour, and coverage pressure is exactly the pressure that produces edits nobody scrutinises as changes. It replaced a real if unreachable guard with a pattern whose cost profile nobody had considered.\n\nThe fix extracts the segment with a positional lookup whose two outcomes are both reachable, since a URL with no separator is its own final segment, and then tests that segment with an anchored pattern. Nothing is left to backtrack over, and no branch is unreachable."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:parsing",security
created_at: "2026-09-02T20:09:03.200Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-02T20:27:56.104Z"
